StorFuzz's FuzzBench fuzzer, in-process -> forkserver, and nothing else.

Applies to fuzzers/storfuzz_fuzzbench_in_process/src/bin/storfuzz_fbconfig.rs,
a verbatim copy of that crate's src/lib.rs after FuzzBench's own
storfuzz_dryrun.patch (see the Dockerfile). The diff below is therefore the
complete difference from the StorFuzz FuzzBench experiments ran:

  - executor   InProcessExecutor + LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput harness
               -> ForkserverExecutor over the trailing `-- target args`
               (SIGKILL on timeout, as the other unibench forkserver arms;
               child output shown only with LIBAFL_FUZZBENCH_DEBUG, as the
               in-process fuzzer silences it)
  - observers  in-process edges / StorFuzz data maps -> the same two maps in
               shared memory, handed over in __AFL_SHM_ID / __STORFUZZ_SHM_ID
  - tokens     autotokens() from the fuzzer's own binary -> the tokens the
               forkserver target sends
  - dropped    LLVMFuzzerInitialize, and the libFuzzer mode that runs the
               files given as arguments; `remaining` is the target instead
  - main()     the binary's entry point calls libafl_main()
  - BytesInput named on the corpus, where the harness used to infer it

